%description:

Known deviation: Tr36873PathLossModel selects the RMa shadowing sigma with a
different breakpoint distance than the one its own RMa path loss uses.

Tr36873PathLossModel::computeRuralMacro3D() switches path-loss slope at

    dBP = 2 pi hBS hUT fc / c

as the specification prescribes, but getShadowingStdDev() inherits the
UMi/UMa breakpoint of TR 36.814 from its base class,

    d'BP = 4 (hBS - 1)(hUT - 1) fc / c

and applies it to RMa and SMa as well. For hBS = 35 m, hUT = 1.5 m and
fc = 0.8 GHz that is 181.5 m against 880.3 m, so a link at 500 m is treated
as below the breakpoint by the path loss and above it by the shadowing.

Tr38901PathLossModel::getShadowingStdDev() computes the 2 pi hBS hUT fc/c
breakpoint itself and is unaffected.

The check below is the RMa case left out of PathLossShadowing.test.

%expected-failure: the RMa shadowing breakpoint does not match the RMa path-loss breakpoint

%includes:
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/stack/phy/channelmodel/Tr36873PathLossModel.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%activity:
NumericChecker c(0.0);
Tr36873PathLossModel m;
ScenarioParams p;

// dBP = 2 pi hBS hUT fc/c = 880.255 m
p = ScenarioParams();
p.scenario = RURAL_MACROCELL;
p.hNodeB = 35;
p.hUe = 1.5;
p.carrierFrequencyGHz = 0.8;
p.apply(m, this);

c.check("873 RMa sigma d2D=300 (below dBP)", m.getShadowingStdDev(305.6, 300, true), 4.0);
c.check("873 RMa sigma d2D=500 (below dBP)", m.getShadowingStdDev(501.1, 500, true), 4.0);
c.check("873 RMa sigma d2D=800 (below dBP)", m.getShadowingStdDev(800.7, 800, true), 4.0);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
checks=3 failures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
